#Formats used for the ZX81 Emulation
#(C) 2024 Ignacio Cea Fornies
?./SINCLAIR.fmt
?./Standard.fmt
#---
;ULARegisters
BORDER:@BORDER@
MIC output:@MICOUT@
EAR output:@EAROUT@
EAR input:@EARIN@
EAR read D6:@EARREAD@
Buzzer:@BUZZER@
#---
#---
;ULASoundFunction
Sampling Frequency:@SAMPLINGFREQ@, Clocks Per Sampling:@CLOCKSSAMPLING@
#---
#---
;ULAVoice
Id:@ID@, Active:@ACTIVE@
->Waves:
@WAVES?{fmter=.CLASS,empty=no waves}\n@
#---
#---
;ULA
Id:@ID@
/INT active:@INTLINE@, ULA clocks remaining:@INTCLOCKS@
@ATTRS?{key=YES,equal=:,empty=no attributes}\n@
->Registers:
@ULARegisters>@
->Control lines:
@Raster>@
->Sound function:
@ULASoundFunction>@
#---
#---
;CULA
@ULA>@
#---
#---
;CULAEVENTS
Legend:
Light Cyan: Screen Starts.
Dark Grey: Reading graphics information.
Light Orange: Content (Access to Video) Situation.
Light Violet: HALT active.
Light Purple: Executing INT interruption.
Light Blue: Executing NMI interruption.
If two events happen in the same visual position, 
only the last one is shown (in this order)
Some events like HALT, INT or NMI mainly may happen out of the visible screen
but they are shown at the beginning of the visible part.
#---
#---
;CSCREENDUMP
@BYTES{blocksize=32,listsep=\,,tablesep=\ ,minsize=2}@
#---
#---
;CCOLORDUMP
@BYTES{blocksize=32,listsep=\,,tablesep=\ ,minsize=2}@
#---
#---
;CCHARSDRAW
@DRAW@
#---
#---
;ZXSpectrumDatasetteInjection
Id:@ID@
@ATTRS?{key=YES,equal=:,empty=no attributes}\n@
COMMANDS:
@COMMANDS@
Keys Pressed:@KEYS@
Motor on:@MOTOR@
Position:@DATACOUNTER@,@ELEMENTCOUNTER@
->Data:
Name:@DATANAME@ (Size:@DATASIZE@)
@DATA?{fmter=DatasetteData,empty=no data}\n---\n@
Number Blocks:@NUMBERBLOCKS@ (Read:@BLOCKTOREAD@)
->Trap:
@TRAP@
#---
#---
;ZXSpectrumPrinterSimulation
Id:@ID@
@ATTRS?{key=YES,equal=:,empty=no attributes}\n@
COMMANDS:
@COMMANDS@
->Traps:
@TRAPS?{key=no,equal=,empty=no trap}\n@
->Matrix Emulation:
@MatrixPrinterEmulation>@
#---